","assessment":"The reviewer asks what the native dialog result means. The local JSDoc already names the returnValue property and separates it from Save status. Retain that clarification.","rationale":"requestClose stores the supplied string in this.returnValue and passes it to the native close request. The function does not return that string as its JavaScript result. Naming the property is more precise than saying only that the value is returned.","recommendation":"reply","validation":"Inspected requestClose and test_nativeCloseRequestsKeepReturnValues with git show. The test checks the supplied cancel value and the default value on a later close. It did not run because the Save descendant is not checked out.","appliedSummary":"","changeSummary":"","state":"ready","changeAccepted":false,"changeReverted":false,"changesAmended":false}
